Firelock is the Firecracker-microVM execution shell extracted from the
Kilimanjaro platform. It confines an untrusted guest to a single
guest-initiated vsock egress and relays that connection to a pluggable
handler. The confinement guarantee is structural; the handler is the
integrator's to supply (a working HTTP reverse-proxy handler ships as the
default so the shell is usable on its own).

